+# Structured SDK lane: a refused formatter result is a repairable contract miss
+
+Branch `fix/structured-finalization`, on top of `42c840cb`.
+Scope touched: `harness/claude_agent_worker.py`, `harness/claude_agent_sdk.py`,
+`tests/test_claude_agent_sdk_formatter_refusal.py` (new),
+`tests/test_claude_agent_sdk_structured.py` (two cases moved/annotated).
+
+## 1. The failure, as recorded
+
+Root review addendum: the documented `MAX_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_RETRIES=0`
+control now disables native format repair before a request starts. Four live
+replays yielded three successes and one schema refusal, each with exactly one
+raw model response. The refused case reached
+`error_max_structured_output_retries` without a second response. The native
+terminal receipt still reported zero usage on that failure, so the measured
+request-side usage remains necessary and output usage remains incomplete.
+Evidence: `structured-retry-zero-probe/{0,1,2,3}/result.json` in the evening
+experiment directory. Reference: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars .
+Earlier conclusions below about the absence of a no-retry control are superseded.
+The choice of default still requires a full coding comparison; these probes
+alone do not establish improved reliability over plain mode.
+
+Six Collie coding attempts in
+`native-structured-v2/native-replay/attempts` produced patches that passed their
+independent graders, but four of them died on a mid/final response with
+
+    RuntimeError: SDK structured formatter reported a failed tool result
+
+(`provider-evidence/NNN-failure.json`, `{"error_type": "RuntimeError"}` — the
+job kept no raw SDK message flow). The four failing requests are
+`event-projection-ledger--collie--00` #009, `--01` #012,
+`snapshot-cursor-pager--collie--00` #015 and `--02` #010: 4 of the 80 structured
+requests those six attempts issued (5.0%). All four are the turn right after
+Harness's "does this fix belong in OTHER files too?" verification reminder.
+
+## 2. Diagnosis: the model's structured output really did miss the schema
+
+Seven one-request replays (of the eight authorized) with the official SDK, the
+sanitized worker env, `claude-opus-5` at `effort=high`, the checked
+`harness.claude_agent_worker._query`, no host tools (init attests
+`tools=["StructuredOutput"]`), safe mode, `max_turns=1`, no settings/MCP.
+Harness under `C:/workspace/collie-benchmark-2026-09-07-evening/structured-final-diagnosis`
+(`replay_structured_failure.py`, `verify_fixed_worker.py`); recorded per case:
+`events.json` (content-free stream types, formatter call shape with prose
+replaced by lengths, formatter receipt, usage) and `outcome.json`.
+
+| replay | formatter input (shape) | receipt | worker |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| ledger--00 #009 | `{"args":{"pattern":"**/*"}, "response":{"tool":"glob","args":{...}}}` | `is_error: true` — `Output does not match required schema: root: must NOT have additional properties` | reproduced the failure |
+| ledger--01 #012 (x2) | `{"response":{"tool":"glob","args":{"pattern":"**/*"}}}` | `Structured output provided successfully` | ok, 148 / 257 output tokens |
+| pager--00 #015 | `{"response":{"response":{"answer":<1216 chars>}}}` | `is_error: true` — `/response: must have required property 'answer', /response: must NOT have additional properties, /response: must have required property 'tool', ... must match a schema in anyOf` | reproduced the failure |
+| pager--02 #010 | `{"response":{"response":{"answer":<1292 chars>}}}` | same refusal report | reproduced the failure |
+
+**Verdict: none of the three candidate causes is a bug in the SDK transport or a
+worker misunderstanding of the stream.** The model called `StructuredOutput`
+exactly once, and its input genuinely violated the requested schema in two
+observed ways — a duplicated top-level `args` beside a correct `response`, and a
+`response` wrapped in a second `response`. The SDK's receipt (`is_error: true`)
+is a correct report of that, and the worker was right to refuse the response.
+The schema itself is valid and accepted (it compiled, and the other 76 requests
+in the same job passed through it); it is not a schema-compatibility error.
+
+Why the provider does not simply prevent these shapes: the bundled CLI derives a
+*strict* input schema for constrained decoding and only uses it when the
+conversion succeeds (`claude.exe`, `rOo`/`tOo`, telemetry
+`tengu_structured_output_strict_schema` `converted`/`fallback`). That conversion
+rejects (a) any node carrying `anyOf` beside `type` (only `$schema`,
+`description`, `title` may accompany `anyOf`) and (b) an object node with no
+`properties` (`reason: "no_properties"`). Collie's envelope hits both: the
+`response` node is `{"type":"object","anyOf":[...]}`, and `args` is deliberately
+an open object because the argument schema is owned by the host executor.
+Closing `args` to satisfy the converter would set `additionalProperties:false`
+on an empty property set, i.e. forbid every tool argument, so **provider-side
+enforcement of this envelope can only ever be post-hoc Ajv validation, not
+constrained decoding**. A small rate of malformed envelopes is therefore
+expected in structured mode, exactly as in plain mode.
+
+So the actual regression is in the reaction, not the detection: plain mode turns
+an unbridgeable envelope into a `response_contract_error` (422) that Harness
+repairs with one corrective turn, while structured mode turned the same event
+into a generic worker exit — unclassifiable (`classify_error` → `terminal`),
+usage lost, run over.
+
+## 3. The fix
+
+`harness/claude_agent_worker.py`
+
+* `_formatter_receipt()` now returns `(tool_use_id, refused)`. Only the literal
+  `True` error flag is a refusal verdict; a non-boolean flag, an unrecognised
+  success receipt, a missing id or a mismatched id all still fail closed exactly
+  as before. The formatter's report text is never read — it quotes the response
+  being refused.
+* On a refusal the worker requires that the raw stream showed exactly one
+  `message_start` and that its id matches the Assistant message, then raises
+  `_StructuredContractRejected` carrying the usage measured at `message_start`
+  and the reviewed auth attestation. **The stream is stopped there**: the SDK's
+  next act is its hidden format-repair turn, and consuming it would spend a
+  second model response no request budget authorized.
+* `main()` turns that into the worker's stdout contract: non-zero exit with
+  `{"ok": false, "structured_error": "formatter_refused_response", "usage": ...,
+  "api_key_source": "none"}`. No refused response, no formatter prose.
+
+`harness/claude_agent_sdk.py`
+
+* `_formatter_refusal(payload)` re-validates that category at the process
+  boundary the same way `_provider_rejection` does (success flag, auth
+  attestation, no assistant content, no provider error, valid usage), and a
+  zero-exit success payload may not also claim a refusal.
+* `complete()` maps it to the same completion the in-band envelope miss already
+  returns: `stop_reason="error"`, `error_status=422`,
+  `error_code="response_contract_error"`, `request_count=1`, usage preserved,
+  reservation settled `completed`, nothing streamed. `classify_error` →
+  `protocol`, so `harness/loop.py` spends its one `FORMAT_REPAIR_NUDGE`
+  corrective turn with no backoff, instead of ending the run.
+* A refusal arriving on a call that requested no schema stays a generic,
+  non-protocol error.
+
+Acceptance is not loosened anywhere: the malformed envelopes above are still
+refused, unmatched or duplicated receipts are still hard failures, and the
+canonical-envelope, one-response-id and structured-output/formatter-input
+equality checks are untouched.
+
+## 4. Usage, and what "measured" means here
+
+`message_start` carries the request side in full (e.g. `input_tokens: 2`,
+`cache_read_input_tokens: 20502`) and an `output_tokens` placeholder (2–3) that
+the provider revises in a later `message_delta`. Replay
+`ledger--01 #012--usage` pins the ordering: `AssistantMessage.usage` is the
+placeholder too, and the revised total (148) only arrives *after* the formatter
+receipt — i.e. only if the stream is left open into the repair turn. So the
+refusal path reports the measured request side and reports the response side as
+**unmeasured (0)** rather than publishing a placeholder as if it were the
+response size. Previously this path reported no usage at all.
+
+## 5. Tests
+
+Focused, offline (`python -m pytest`, this worktree):
+
+* `tests/test_claude_agent_sdk_formatter_refusal.py` (new, 30 cases): the
+  classified refusal and its preserved usage; the refused response, the report
+  and `**/*` never appearing in any surfaced string; the repair turn never being
+  consumed (asserted by message count against a scripted second model turn);
+  fail-closed on 0/2 `message_start`s, on unmatched/blank receipt ids, and on
+  non-boolean error flags; `main()`'s payload and exit code; the boundary
+  recogniser and nine forged payloads; the real `_run_worker` over a fake
+  non-zero-exit process; the completion's code/status/accounting/`protocol`
+  classification, plus the plain-mode guard.
+* `tests/test_claude_agent_sdk_structured.py`: the `is_error=True` row moved out
+  of the fail-closed table (it is now the classified path); the
+  flag-not-coerced test kept and annotated.
+* Ran: `test_claude_agent_sdk_formatter_refusal.py`,
+  `test_claude_agent_sdk_structured.py`, `test_claude_agent_sdk.py`,
+  `test_claude_agent_sdk_provider_error.py`,
+  `test_claude_agent_sdk_product_entry.py` → **195 passed, 2 skipped**;
+  `test_loop.py`, `test_providers.py` → **90 passed**. The full suite was not
+  run (out of scope for this change).
+
+Live, with the fixed worker spawned exactly as the transport spawns it
+(`python -I harness/claude_agent_worker.py`, sanitized env, recorded request on
+stdin): `pager--02 #010` → valid `{"answer": ...}`, 856 output tokens;
+`ledger--00 #009` → valid `{"tool": "glob", "args": {"pattern": "**/*"}}`, 150
+output tokens (`structured-final-diagnosis/fixed-worker--*.json`). Both are
+happy-path non-regression evidence and both re-sampled *the same contexts that
+refused earlier*, which is the same thing the corrective turn does.
+
+## 6. Limitations and residual risk
+
+1. **The refusal path itself was not exercised live end-to-end.** It is
+   stochastic (3 refusals in 7 samples of these four adversarial requests) and
+   cannot be forced without changing the prompt, which is not allowed. The live
+   evidence is the four replays in §2 (which show the exact stream the fix
+   classifies) plus the offline tests; the two post-fix live runs happened to
+   sample valid envelopes.
+2. **A hidden repair request may already be in flight when we stop.** The worker
+   stops at the receipt and the transport kills the process tree, but the CLI
+   decides to repair before it emits the tool result to us. Nothing observable
+   from this side can prove whether that HTTP request left the machine. This is
+   unchanged by the fix (the old code raised at the same point); it is the
+   reason the stream is not drained for the revised usage. If the SDK ever gains
+   a "no format repair" option, that is the real close-out.
+3. **Output tokens on a refusal are reported as 0** (§4) — an understatement,
+   deliberately preferred to publishing a placeholder.
+4. **One sibling failure mode is still generic.** When the model emits the
+   envelope as *text* instead of calling the formatter, the CLI injects a
+   `[structured-output-enforce]` user message (constant `X0o` in the bundled
+   CLI; observed in `structured-failure-diagnostic/` before `b8004abd`), and the
+   worker fails with "SDK emitted a tool result before the structured formatter
+   call". That is the same class of event and could be classified the same way,
+   but it did not recur in this job and recognising it means matching
+   CLI-generated marker prose, so it is left fail-closed rather than fixed
+   unverified.
+5. **Structured mode is left on by default.** With this fix its worst case is
+   the plain lane's worst case — one corrective turn, ~5% of requests in this
+   job — and it removed the extra-key free-text failures that motivated it, so
+   an opt-in default is not warranted. The escape hatch already exists if the
+   host disagrees: `ClaudeAgentSdkProvider(structured_output=False)` restores
+   the byte-identical plain request.
+6. `max_contract_repairs` (default 1) governs recovery; a refusal on the
+   corrective turn as well still ends the run.
+7. The replay/verification scripts live outside the repo, under
+   `structured-final-diagnosis/`, and are not shipped or imported by Collie.
